<h1><span lang="EN-GB">On Rotate/Pan Display Normal</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from the <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>viewport context menu &gt; On Rotate/Pan &gt; Display Normal</b></span> or by setting the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Normal</b></span> option in <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>System &gt; Preferences / Display / Rotate/Pan/Zoom</b></span> dialog.</p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">On Rotate/Pan Display Normal</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command affects visualisation of scan data, meshes, and point clouds in the scene during rotate, pan, and zoom actions and is related to the details of objects.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">It is not applicable when</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command" style="text-decoration:none;">On Rotate/Pan Draw Scene</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">is enabled. Selecting this command will cause KUBE to display every 10-th point during rotate, pan, and zoom.</span> It is equivalent to the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Normal</b></span> option located in <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Number of points</b></span> group from <a href="Display_Settings_-_On_Rotate_Pan.htm">Preferences / Display</a> dialog. <span lang="EN-GB">This mode is by default and is stored so next time when you run KUBE</span> <span class="Mode">Display Normal</span> <span lang="EN-GB">will be used.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
